{
 "__comment": "S-117 (ruling 248). CAPTURED FROM THE LIVE `/audit_logs/recent`, not written by hand: the three shapes a ledger receipt takes, exactly as the route emits them. The timeline draws these with no new route and no new table - `column_name` is the mechanism word `ledger_batch`, which is what a kind filter keys on.",
 "__notes": {
  "grouping": "`transaction_id` is the transaction of the change that CAUSED the batch, so a receipt appears in the same group as the edit that triggered it.",
  "empty_transaction_id": "The log's `transaction_id` is null and the ROUTE buckets it under the group key 'no_tid'. That null is a VALUE, not a gap: it says a backfill or a retroactive run produced this batch rather than somebody's edit. Do not fold it in with rows that are missing data.",
  "is_row_deleted": "true on every receipt, and it is not about deletion: `row_id` is the BATCH's id, so no row of the table carries it and the existence probe says so. A receipt must not be drawn as a deleted row.",
  "failed": "one receipt PER SOURCE that could not be followed, sharing the transaction id of the event. Written in a commit of its own, because the batch's own rolled back and took any receipt inside it.",
  "worlds": "followed_in_two_worlds and one_world_failed (2026-10-04): captured on the isolated PostgreSQL scratch schema (server 6922cd6cb) through the route functions behind /audit_logs/transaction/{tx}, not the box: one edit followed in two live worlds - a receipt per world, each with `world`, beside the edit itself - and the same edit with the branch world's translation made to raise (its failure receipt names the world too). The branch world's name is the test's own. `is_row_deleted` is false on a receipt since 218f907f5.",
  "recent_groups": "recent_group_* (2026-10-06, re-captured the same day): captured on the isolated PostgreSQL scratch schema (server c49217a06; re-captured with the lead's two history-list changes) through the route function behind /audit_logs/recent - the list's own group shape: ONE representative log - the newest that is not a ledger receipt, so here the edit itself; a group of receipts only shows its newest - the transaction's summary_columns, and receipt_worlds (each world its receipts were written into, in the order written, and `failed`: how many of them say that world's translation failed). The same two transactions as followed_in_two_worlds / one_world_failed, read from the list."
 },
